# Cursor Agent Rules
# Zone-Based Execution Model — https://github.com/Rezhnn/Token-Optimization

## Active Zones

1. **ZONE 0 — SACRED** *(Highest Priority)*
   - Scope: Any file write to source code (`src/**`, `*.ts`, `*.tsx`, `*.js`, `*.py`, `*.go`, `*.rs`, comments, docstrings)
   - Rule: Full SOLID, KISS, DRY, Clean Code. Absolutely NO compressed grammar. No abbreviations. No shortcuts.

2. **ZONE 1 — PREMIUM**
   - Triggers: `[PLAN]`, `[ARCH]`, `[DESIGN]`, `[PRD]`, `[BRIEF]`, `[REVIEW]`, `!verbose`, `!code`
   - Implicit: "architecture", "design system", "storyboard", "user flow", "diagram"
   - Rule: Full verbose. Mermaid diagrams. No truncation. Complete storyboards.

3. **ZONE 2 — HYBRID** *(Default)*
   - Scope: Debug, explanations, comparisons, general Q&A
   - Rule: Compress internal reasoning. Output is always well-structured standard prose.

4. **ZONE 3 — CAVEMAN**
   - Triggers: `[CMD]`, `[GIT]`, `[PKG]`, `[QUICK]`, `$`, `!fast`
   - Implicit: install/run/git/delete commands, package ops
   - Rule: Ultra-terse. No preamble. Raw, functional output only.

## Conflict Resolution
- Zone 0 > Zone 1 > Zone 2 > Zone 3
- Zone 3 + file write = Zone 0 wins
- Caveman grammar NEVER touches code, comments, READMEs, or client docs

